   "failure_category": "wrong_answer",
   "final_answer": "It appears that there is an issue with the SQL query due to an ambiguous column name. Let's try running the query again with a more specific approach to avoid this error. We will fetch the conversion rates for the control and treatment groups and calculate the relative lift based on the provided guidelines.\n\nHere is the SQL query to fetch the conversion rates:\n```sql\nSELECT \n    variant, \n    CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN event = 'conversion' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS REAL) / COUNT(*) AS conversion_rate \nFROM \n    experiment_assignments \nJOIN \n    experiment_events ON experiment_assignments.id = experiment_events.experiment_id \nWHERE \n    experiment_id IN (SELECT id FROM experiments WHERE key = 'checkout_redesign') \nGROUP BY \n    variant \nORDER BY \n    variant;\n```\n\nOnce we have the conversion rates, we can calculate the relative lift as follows:\n- Control Rate: The proportion of users in the control group who converted.\n- Treatment Rate: The proportion of users in the treatment group who converted.\n- Relative Lift: (Treatment Rate / Control Rate) - 1\n\nLet's execute the query and calculate the relative lift."
